---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../../../components/ui/button/Button.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import AnnotatedFigure from "../../../../components/inspector/AnnotatedFigure.astro";
import Icon from "../../../../components/ui/icon/Icon.astro";
import InspectorCollage from "../../../../components/InspectorCollage.astro";
import Kbd from "../../../../components/ui/kbd/Kbd.astro";
import Link from "../../../../components/ui/link/Link.astro";
import MarkdownH1 from "../../../../components/MarkdownH1.astro";
import MarkdownH2 from "../../../../components/MarkdownH2.astro";
import MarkdownList from "../../../../components/MarkdownList.astro";
import Table from "../../../../components/ui/table/Table.astro";
import TableCell from "../../../../components/ui/table/TableCell.astro";
import TableHead from "../../../../components/ui/table/TableHead.astro";
import TableRow from "../../../../components/ui/table/TableRow.astro";
import Prose from "../../../../components/Prose.astro";
import TerminalCommands from "../../../../components/TerminalCommands.astro";

import { desktopBottomSlot, inspectorCollage, opencodeInspector } from "../../../../config/opencode-inspector";
import { projectLinks } from "../../../../config/site";

const source = `${projectLinks.github}/tree/main/integrations/opencode/inspector`;
const serverPluginConfig = `{
	"plugins": ["${opencodeInspector.package}"]
}`;
const tuiPluginConfig = `{
	"plugins": [
		{
			"package": "${opencodeInspector.package}",
			"options": {
				"rows": 2,
				"current": "glyph"
			}
		}
	]
}`;
---

<BaseLayout title='OpenCode task inspector' description={opencodeInspector.description}>
	<div class='site-container py-8 md:py-12'>
		<Breadcrumbs />

		<section class='pb-9 md:pb-12'>
			<MarkdownH1>{opencodeInspector.title}</MarkdownH1>
			<div class='grid gap-7 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] md:items-end md:gap-12'>
				<p class='max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed'>Experimental. {opencodeInspector.description}</p>
				<div class='flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:justify-end'>
					<Button href='#installation' variant='solid' size='large'>Installation</Button>
					<Button href={source} variant='outline' size='large'>Source</Button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<InspectorCollage
			base={inspectorCollage.base}
			width={inspectorCollage.width}
			height={inspectorCollage.height}
			caption={inspectorCollage.caption}
			parts={inspectorCollage.parts}
			class='mb-12 md:mb-16'
		/>

		<div class='max-w-3xl'>
			<Prose>
				<p>
					The inspector reads tasks, labels and recorded activity through the local Zinn CLI. It uses the same <a
						href='/docs/settings'>data directory and settings</a
					> as the CLI running in that environment. It loads active tasks from the default project, or from every project
					when no default is set. With a remote OpenCode server, the TUI inspector still runs locally and reads the local
					CLI's database. OpenCode Desktop also shows an experimental board summary for the default project.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Requirements</MarkdownH2>
				<MarkdownList>
					<li>OpenCode {opencodeInspector.verifiedVersion}.</li>
					<li>
						Zinn CLI {opencodeInspector.minimumCliVersion} or newer on the terminal's <code>PATH</code>, with a database
						it can read.
					</li>
					<li>The inspector package <code>{opencodeInspector.package}</code>.</li>
				</MarkdownList>

				<MarkdownH2 id='installation'>Install</MarkdownH2>
				<p>Install the package in two OpenCode configuration files, keeping any existing plugin entries.</p>
				<p>
					Add it to <code>~/.config/opencode/opencode.json</code> for the server and desktop entries:
				</p>
				<TerminalCommands label='opencode.json' commands={[serverPluginConfig]} showsPrompt={false} />
				<p>
					Add the same package to <code>~/.config/opencode/cli.json</code> with the inspector options:
				</p>
				<TerminalCommands label='cli.json' commands={[tuiPluginConfig]} showsPrompt={false} />
				<p>
					OpenCode loads the server and desktop entries from <code>opencode.json</code> and the TUI inspector from{" "}
					<code>cli.json</code>. Both entries use the same spec, so they share one package download. The{" "}
					<code>cli.json</code> object carries the TUI options. OpenCode applies <code>opencode.json</code> options to the
					server and desktop entries, not to the TUI inspector.
				</p>
				<p>
					OpenCode loads these entries through its native <Link href='https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/cli/plugins/'
						>plugin configuration</Link
					>. Start OpenCode, open a conversation and mention a task key from your database. Select the task to inspect
					it.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Find and inspect tasks</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Run <code>/zinn</code> to find a loaded active task. The command palette also offers{" "}
					<strong>Zinn: task keys in this chat</strong> and{" "}
					<strong>Zinn: pick a task from the board</strong>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Task details include status, priority, labels, the first paragraph of the description, relations, comment
					count and a short excerpt of the latest mention in the conversation. When the detail is opened from a task key
					mentioned in this chat, it also says how many times that task was mentioned. Select a related task to open it
					in the same dialog, then use back to return. Long relation lists scroll in place. Close the dialog with its
					close control or <Kbd>Esc</Kbd>. Unknown keys are shown when their project prefix appears among the loaded
					tasks. Select the ZINN heading to refresh task and label data.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Desktop board summary</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					OpenCode Desktop shows a board summary in the bottom slot. It follows the default project's board with the
					active task total, the count in each column with tasks, and when the board was last read. Columns with <strong
						>done</strong
					> category are colored green. Backlog and cancelled ones are dimmed.
				</p>
				<p>
					The strip reads the board in the current session's directory. A successful read stamps <code
						>synced HH:MM</code
					>. A failed read keeps the last counts and stamps <code>no read</code>, with the error on hover.
				</p>
				<p>
					The ZINN wordmark opens the Zinn documentation. The Zinn settings page turns the strip on or off and sets the
					refresh interval to 30 seconds, 1 minute, 5 minutes or 15 minutes. The default is 1 minute.
				</p>
			</Prose>
		</div>

		<AnnotatedFigure {...desktopBottomSlot} class='my-12 md:my-16' />

		<div class='max-w-3xl'>
			<Prose>
				<MarkdownH2 id='options'>Options</MarkdownH2>
				<Table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<TableHead>Option</TableHead>
							<TableHead>Default</TableHead>
							<TableHead>Behavior</TableHead>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<TableRow>
							<TableCell><code>rows</code></TableCell>
							<TableCell><code>1</code></TableCell>
							<TableCell>
								Accepts <code>1</code> or <code>2</code>. <code>2</code> includes column, priority and labels.
							</TableCell>
						</TableRow>
						<TableRow>
							<TableCell><code>current</code></TableCell>
							<TableCell><code>"off"</code></TableCell>
							<TableCell>
								Accepts <code>"off"</code> or <code>"glyph"</code>. <code>"glyph"</code> marks tasks with recorded activity
								from this conversation family.
							</TableCell>
						</TableRow>
					</tbody>
				</Table>

				<MarkdownH2>Conversation marks</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					A conversation mark means a task has recorded activity whose session or thread ID matches the current
					conversation, its root or one of its children. A mention alone does not create a mark. The mark records
					activity, rather than an assignment or ownership claim.
				</p>
				<p>
					OpenCode's native shell session ID is recorded by Zinn as a thread ID. An explicit{" "}
					<code>ZINN_SESSION_ID</code> and <code>ZINN_THREAD_ID</code> pair takes precedence. The inspector recognizes both
					routes. See <Link href='/docs/cli/identity#who-am-i'>actor identity</Link> for the CLI contract.
				</p>
				<p>
					The mark animates while OpenCode reports that conversation as busy. Busy state comes from the host
					independently of the task's recorded activity. Tasks in Done keep their green treatment.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Compatibility</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Version {opencodeInspector.version} targets OpenCode 2.3.x, verified on {opencodeInspector.verifiedVersion},
					and its OpenTUI {opencodeInspector.openTuiVersion} runtime. The <code>^0.5.0</code> entry installs 0.5.x patches.
					Move to a new inspector minor only when its release notes name the OpenCode version it supports.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Update</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					OpenCode updates the package from the <code>opencode.json</code> entry. In OpenCode Desktop, open Settings › Extensions
					› Plugins, select Check for updates, then Update on the package. In the terminal, run
					<code>opencode plugin check</code> and <code>opencode plugin update</code>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Both entries use the same spec, so an update installs the new 0.5.x package for both. Restart OpenCode to load
					the new TUI inspector and desktop entry. An exact version is skipped by the update check, so keep the
					<code>^0.5.0</code> range.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Remove</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Remove the package entry from each configuration file where you added it, then start OpenCode again. Your Zinn
					projects, tasks and activity remain in the database.
				</p>
			</Prose>

			<div class='mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5 border-t border-pewter pt-6'>
				<p class='font-mono text-xs'>Verified with OpenCode {opencodeInspector.verifiedVersion}</p>
				<a class='inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs' href={source}
					>Inspector source <Icon name='external-link' /></a
				>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
